 "reading_rule": "Discharges in m3/s and km3 a year (a Julian year). A mouth is a cell of the receiving water that a channel enters; its basin is the land draining through it. Places are [latitude, longitude east] in degrees on today's Moon and on the turned Moon of the frame record. to_other_waters_m3s is the discharge reaching outlet waters other than the seas listed. hollows_filling lists the hollows, other than the six seas, that take 5,000 m3/s or more of river water at the common level, and smaller_seas_filling the four smaller seas in the two_seas run: the height above the common level at which each basin spills (the level of the depressions under its cells, as the area-weighted median with its lowest and highest values), its area at the common level, the area that spill level floods and the volume of water between the two levels.",
